{%- comment -%}
  Outputs the sort key a collection opens in: the store default, the All
  products default for /collections/all, or `manual` for a collection listed in
  "Collections in their own order" (Settings → Collection), whose order is set
  in Shopify admin — Trending, which a daily job re-ranks, is the reason.

  One place for this, because every collection link carries `sort_by` (see
  main-collection.liquid) and they all have to agree with the page itself.

  Accepts one of:
  - sort_collection: {Object} The collection.
  - sort_url:        {String} A collection URL, for menu links.
  And optionally:
  - default_sort:    {String} Overrides the store default.
  - all_sort:        {String} Overrides the All products default.

  Named `sort_collection` rather than `collection` so the page's own
  collection, which snippets can see, is never picked up by mistake.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sort = default_sort | default: settings.collection_default_sort | default: 'best-selling'

  assign is_all = false
  if sort_collection != blank and sort_collection.handle == 'all'
    assign is_all = true
  elsif sort_url != blank and sort_url == routes.all_products_collection_url
    assign is_all = true
  endif
  if is_all
    assign sort = all_sort | default: settings.collection_all_default_sort | default: sort
  endif

  for own in settings.collection_own_order
    if sort_collection != blank and own.id == sort_collection.id
      assign sort = 'manual'
      break
    elsif sort_url != blank and own.url == sort_url
      assign sort = 'manual'
      break
    endif
  endfor

  echo sort
-%}
